  "title": "Erdős Problem #954",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $1=a_1<a_2<\\cdots$ be the sequence of integers defined by $a_1=1$ and $a_{k+1}$ is the smallest integer $n$ for which the number of solutions to $a_i+a_j \\leq n$ (with $i\\leq j\\leq k$) is less than $n-k$.\nIs the number of solutions to $a_i+a_j \\leq x$ equal to $x+O(x^{1/4+o(1)})$?",
